nsncd (1.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  nsncd now runs as the unprivileged sysytem user and grou `_nsncd`
  which the package creates on install. The service unit also applied
  systemd sandboxing; it drops all capabilities and enabled
  ProtectSystem=strict, PrivateTmp and RestrictAddressFamiliies.

  Most NSS modules work unchanged, including ss,s ldacp (nslcd), winbind,
  systemd, files, extrausers and cache, because they read world-reasable
  files or talk to a privileged daemon over a socket.

